1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,382
You wash your windows, and they dry with

2
00:00:02,392 --> 00:00:05,270
streaks, smears and cloudy patches.

3
00:00:05,631 --> 00:00:08,602
The mistake is in the method, not the
cleaner.

4
00:00:09,056 --> 00:00:12,424
Seven steps to get glass crystal clear,
inside

5
00:00:12,434 --> 00:00:14,767
and out, with simple supplies.

6
00:00:15,917 --> 00:00:20,119
Stay for step five: it's the move the
professionals use.

7
00:00:20,733 --> 00:00:21,672
WikiTube.

8
00:00:21,905 --> 00:00:24,180
Whatever it is, here's how.

9
00:00:24,467 --> 00:00:28,448
Streaks have three causes: cleaning in
direct sun,

10
00:00:28,809 --> 00:00:31,806
so the liquid dries too fast; too much

11
00:00:31,816 --> 00:00:35,103
cleaner, which leaves a film; and the
wrong

12
00:00:35,113 --> 00:00:37,295
cloth, which leaves lint.

13
00:00:38,445 --> 00:00:40,827
Fix those three, and a bucket and a

14
00:00:40,837 --> 00:00:42,136
squeegee are enough.

15
00:00:43,101 --> 00:00:45,900
Never lean out of upper-floor windows, or
use

16
00:00:45,910 --> 00:00:47,605
a ladder without help.

17
00:00:48,167 --> 00:00:50,409
You'll need a bucket of warm water, a

18
00:00:50,419 --> 00:00:52,928
drop of dish soap, a squeegee with a

19
00:00:52,938 --> 00:00:57,027
clean blade, microfiber cloths, and, if
you like,

20
00:00:57,037 --> 00:00:59,277
white vinegar for spot cleaning.

21
00:00:59,833 --> 00:01:00,784
Step one.

22
00:01:01,075 --> 00:01:03,468
Choose a cloudy day, or work in the

23
00:01:03,478 --> 00:01:07,056
shade, because direct sun dries the
cleaner before

24
00:01:07,066 --> 00:01:09,584
you can wipe it, and leaves streaks.

25
00:01:09,945 --> 00:01:11,721
Avoid freezing weather, too.

26
00:01:12,685 --> 00:01:15,833
Gather all your supplies before you start,
so

27
00:01:15,843 --> 00:01:17,851
you don't have to leave with wet hands.

28
00:01:19,001 --> 00:01:20,930
Lay a towel on the sill and floor

29
00:01:20,940 --> 00:01:22,158
to catch drips.

30
00:01:22,612 --> 00:01:24,866
Work on windows you can safely reach from

31
00:01:24,876 --> 00:01:27,870
the ground, indoors or outdoors.

32
00:01:28,417 --> 00:01:30,253
Open the window slightly if you want to

33
00:01:30,263 --> 00:01:31,609
clean the frame edges.

34
00:01:32,062 --> 00:01:35,593
Also, remove curtains, plants and
ornaments from the

35
00:01:35,603 --> 00:01:39,782
sill beforehand, so nothing gets wet or
knocked over.

36
00:01:40,333 --> 00:01:41,423
Step two.

37
00:01:41,970 --> 00:01:44,212
Use a dry brush or a vacuum with

38
00:01:44,222 --> 00:01:47,823
a soft attachment to remove cobwebs, dust
and

39
00:01:47,833 --> 00:01:51,617
loose dirt from the frame, the sill and
the corners.

40
00:01:52,279 --> 00:01:55,135
Wipe the edges of the glass with a dry
cloth.

41
00:01:55,797 --> 00:01:58,295
If you skip this, the water will turn

42
00:01:58,305 --> 00:02:01,694
the dust to muddy streaks that run down
the glass.

43
00:02:02,055 --> 00:02:04,251
Take a moment to clear the window track

44
00:02:04,261 --> 00:02:06,675
too, where dirt collects.

45
00:02:07,338 --> 00:02:11,389
Cleaning from the top down avoids dripping
on cleaned areas.

46
00:02:11,749 --> 00:02:14,038
This takes two minutes, but it makes the

47
00:02:14,048 --> 00:02:17,902
whole job much cleaner and prevents you
from smearing dirt.

48
00:02:18,565 --> 00:02:21,620
Next comes the cleaning solution, and it
needs

49
00:02:21,630 --> 00:02:23,718
less soap than you might think.

50
00:02:24,267 --> 00:02:25,323
Step three.

51
00:02:25,684 --> 00:02:27,973
Fill a bucket with about a gallon, or

52
00:02:27,983 --> 00:02:31,084
four litres, of warm water, and add just

53
00:02:31,094 --> 00:02:32,742
a few drops of dish soap.

54
00:02:33,405 --> 00:02:34,751
Less is better.

55
00:02:35,901 --> 00:02:38,965
Too much soap leaves a film that causes
streaks.

56
00:02:39,419 --> 00:02:42,924
For a spray-bottle alternative, mix equal
parts water

57
00:02:42,983 --> 00:02:44,201
and white vinegar.

58
00:02:45,003 --> 00:02:47,649
This works well on lightly dirty glass.

59
00:02:48,103 --> 00:02:51,216
Avoid vinegar on natural stone sills, and
test

60
00:02:51,226 --> 00:02:52,642
it on rubber seals.

61
00:02:53,792 --> 00:02:56,833
Never mix vinegar with bleach or ammonia.

62
00:02:57,194 --> 00:02:59,529
Some people add a splash of rubbing
alcohol

63
00:02:59,539 --> 00:03:02,420
in winter, which helps the glass dry
quickly

64
00:03:02,430 --> 00:03:03,613
in cold weather.

65
00:03:04,167 --> 00:03:05,211
Step four.

66
00:03:06,176 --> 00:03:09,718
Dip a microfiber cloth or a
sponge-and-scrubber tool

67
00:03:09,728 --> 00:03:12,804
into the solution, and wring it out
lightly.

68
00:03:13,768 --> 00:03:16,463
Wipe the whole pane from top to bottom,

69
00:03:16,473 --> 00:03:19,003
using firm strokes to lift dirt.

70
00:03:20,154 --> 00:03:24,379
Pay attention to the corners and edges,
where grime collects.

71
00:03:25,529 --> 00:03:28,700
For stubborn spots like bird droppings,
hold the

72
00:03:28,710 --> 00:03:30,639
wet cloth on the spot for a minute

73
00:03:30,649 --> 00:03:31,797
to soften them.

74
00:03:32,599 --> 00:03:36,987
Don't use abrasive scrubbers on glass,
which can cause scratches.

75
00:03:37,649 --> 00:03:40,261
Keep the glass wet until you squeegee.

76
00:03:40,621 --> 00:03:42,957
If the window is very dirty, wash it

77
00:03:42,967 --> 00:03:46,068
twice, because the first pass lifts the
heavy

78
00:03:46,078 --> 00:03:48,759
dirt and the second gets the rest.

79
00:03:49,561 --> 00:03:53,171
Now for the squeegee, the step that makes
the difference.

80
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:54,812
Step five.

81
00:03:55,173 --> 00:03:57,450
Start at the top corner, and pull the

82
00:03:57,460 --> 00:04:00,690
squeegee down in one straight stroke, or
use

83
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:03,206
a gentle S-shape across the glass.

84
00:04:03,753 --> 00:04:06,065
Wipe the rubber blade with a clean cloth

85
00:04:06,075 --> 00:04:07,572
after every pass.

86
00:04:08,374 --> 00:04:10,915
Overlap each stroke by an inch.

87
00:04:11,462 --> 00:04:13,728
Leave a small strip at the bottom, and

88
00:04:13,738 --> 00:04:15,873
wipe the final line with a cloth.

89
00:04:16,837 --> 00:04:19,916
A clean, sharp rubber blade is key to

90
00:04:19,926 --> 00:04:21,353
a perfect result.

91
00:04:22,317 --> 00:04:25,428
If the blade is cracked or worn, replace
it.

92
00:04:26,578 --> 00:04:28,737
Practise on a small window first.

93
00:04:29,190 --> 00:04:32,036
The motion feels natural after a few
strokes,

94
00:04:32,046 --> 00:04:34,147
and the results look professional.

95
00:04:34,700 --> 00:04:35,732
Step six.

96
00:04:36,023 --> 00:04:38,695
Use a dry microfiber cloth to wipe the

97
00:04:38,705 --> 00:04:41,307
edges of the glass, the frame and the

98
00:04:41,317 --> 00:04:43,638
sill, where water gathers.

99
00:04:43,929 --> 00:04:46,299
Then polish any drops or marks on the

100
00:04:46,309 --> 00:04:49,164
pane with another dry, lint-free cloth.

101
00:04:49,966 --> 00:04:52,961
For an inside window, use a light touch.

102
00:04:53,508 --> 00:04:57,747
Avoid paper towels and newspaper, which
leave lint, or

103
00:04:57,757 --> 00:04:58,383
ink.

104
00:04:59,533 --> 00:05:01,601
Step back and look at the glass from

105
00:05:01,611 --> 00:05:06,269
an angle, and from outside and inside,

106
00:05:06,279 --> 00:05:08,019
to spot any streaks.

107
00:05:08,566 --> 00:05:11,839
A damp cloth then removes any final
smudges.

108
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:14,988
Always check both sides of the glass,
because

109
00:05:14,998 --> 00:05:17,040
streaks may be on the other side.

110
00:05:18,005 --> 00:05:20,561
One step is left, and it covers the

111
00:05:20,571 --> 00:05:22,172
parts people forget.

112
00:05:22,733 --> 00:05:23,789
Step seven.

113
00:05:24,754 --> 00:05:27,086
Finish with the parts people forget.

114
00:05:28,051 --> 00:05:30,908
Vacuum the window track, then wipe it with

115
00:05:30,918 --> 00:05:33,727
a cloth dipped in warm soapy water.

116
00:05:34,181 --> 00:05:37,709
A cotton swab or a toothbrush reaches the
corners.

117
00:05:38,674 --> 00:05:41,264
Remove the screens, and rinse them gently
with

118
00:05:41,274 --> 00:05:44,072
a hose, or brush them with soapy water,

119
00:05:44,305 --> 00:05:46,800
then let them dry before replacing them.

120
00:05:47,346 --> 00:05:49,737
Then wipe the sills and frames.

121
00:05:50,284 --> 00:05:53,095
Clean windows every three to four months,
or

122
00:05:53,105 --> 00:05:56,343
when they look dull, and the job will
remain quick.

123
00:05:56,704 --> 00:05:58,853
A quick wipe once a month stops dirt

124
00:05:58,863 --> 00:06:01,199
from building up, and makes the next big

125
00:06:01,209 --> 00:06:03,054
clean much faster.

126
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:07,163
If streaks remain, work out which side
they are on.

127
00:06:08,128 --> 00:06:11,299
Wipe the inside with horizontal strokes
and the

128
00:06:11,309 --> 00:06:13,537
outside with vertical strokes.

129
00:06:13,991 --> 00:06:16,361
The direction of a streak then tells you

130
00:06:16,371 --> 00:06:17,833
which side to fix.

131
00:06:18,983 --> 00:06:22,189
Streaks usually mean too much soap, a
dirty

132
00:06:22,199 --> 00:06:25,275
blade or cloth, or hard water.

133
00:06:26,239 --> 00:06:29,097
For hard water spots, wipe with a cloth

134
00:06:29,107 --> 00:06:31,533
dampened with white vinegar and water.

135
00:06:31,824 --> 00:06:35,262
Do not wash microfiber cloths with fabric
softener,

136
00:06:35,272 --> 00:06:36,908
because it leaves a film.

137
00:06:37,467 --> 00:06:40,392
Some windows are better left to
professionals.

138
00:06:40,845 --> 00:06:44,040
Upper-floor windows, and any glass you can
only

139
00:06:44,050 --> 00:06:47,497
reach by leaning out, are a fall risk.

140
00:06:48,299 --> 00:06:51,145
Fog or moisture trapped between the two
panes

141
00:06:51,155 --> 00:06:54,025
of a double-pane window means the seal has

142
00:06:54,035 --> 00:06:56,994
failed, and cleaning cannot fix it.

143
00:06:57,959 --> 00:07:01,362
Paint overspray and etching from hard
water also

144
00:07:01,372 --> 00:07:03,101
need an expert's tools.

145
00:07:03,462 --> 00:07:05,518
A pro can tell you whether the glass

146
00:07:05,528 --> 00:07:06,735
can be saved.

147
00:07:07,300 --> 00:07:09,970
A few habits keep glass clear longer.

148
00:07:10,423 --> 00:07:13,223
Wipe fingerprints and smudges right away
with a

149
00:07:13,233 --> 00:07:15,159
damp microfiber cloth.

150
00:07:15,520 --> 00:07:18,656
Wash your cloths without fabric softener,
and let

151
00:07:18,666 --> 00:07:19,861
them air dry.

152
00:07:20,408 --> 00:07:22,221
Clean the glass a couple of times a

153
00:07:22,231 --> 00:07:25,806
year, and the screens and tracks at the
same time.

154
00:07:26,608 --> 00:07:30,278
Wipe away condensation on cold mornings,
so mold

155
00:07:30,288 --> 00:07:31,471
does not start.

156
00:07:32,134 --> 00:07:34,620
Keep a small squeegee near the bathroom
window

157
00:07:34,630 --> 00:07:35,964
for quick wipes.

158
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:38,728
Here are the mistakes to avoid.

159
00:07:39,879 --> 00:07:42,803
First, cleaning in direct sunlight.

160
00:07:43,606 --> 00:07:46,277
The liquid dries before you can wipe, and

161
00:07:46,287 --> 00:07:48,051
the sun gives you streaks.

162
00:07:49,015 --> 00:07:51,813
Second, using too much soap or cleaner.

163
00:07:52,266 --> 00:07:55,690
A little is enough, and more only leaves a
film.

164
00:07:56,353 --> 00:08:00,648
And third, using dirty cloths or a dirty
squeegee blade.

165
00:08:01,009 --> 00:08:03,655
They spread dirt, rather than lifting it.

166
00:08:04,317 --> 00:08:07,326
For upper floors, hire a professional or
use

167
00:08:07,336 --> 00:08:10,240
a proper extension pole, and never lean
out

168
00:08:10,250 --> 00:08:11,178
of a window.

169
00:08:11,841 --> 00:08:14,756
Be careful with glass edges and ladders,
and

170
00:08:14,766 --> 00:08:17,146
ask for help whenever you can.

171
00:08:17,700 --> 00:08:18,802
Let's recap.

172
00:08:19,163 --> 00:08:22,343
Pick the right time, and gather your
supplies.

173
00:08:23,308 --> 00:08:25,570
Dust the frame and the glass.

174
00:08:25,745 --> 00:08:28,914
Mix a simple solution with just a little
soap.

175
00:08:30,064 --> 00:08:31,456
Wash the glass.

176
00:08:32,421 --> 00:08:34,359
Squeegee in clean strokes.

177
00:08:34,592 --> 00:08:36,611
Dry the edges and polish.

178
00:08:37,762 --> 00:08:40,164
And clean the tracks and screens.

179
00:08:40,966 --> 00:08:43,487
Seven steps, about an hour for a whole

180
00:08:43,497 --> 00:08:46,204
house, and windows that let the light in.

181
00:08:46,214 --> 00:08:50,581
Bonus sections cover how to track

182
00:08:50,591 --> 00:08:54,235
down stubborn streaks, when to call a
professional,

183
00:08:54,468 --> 00:08:56,952
and how to keep windows clear longer.

184
00:08:57,500 --> 00:09:01,612
That's how you clean windows without
streaks, inside and

185
00:09:01,622 --> 00:09:02,178
out.

186
00:09:02,841 --> 00:09:06,462
If your windows are sparkling, subscribe
to WikiTube,

187
00:09:06,637 --> 00:09:09,887
because we publish a new how-to every
single day.

188
00:09:10,248 --> 00:09:11,851
Tell us in the comments what you want

189
00:09:11,861 --> 00:09:14,740
us to clean next, and see you tomorrow.

190
00:09:14,833 --> 00:09:16,039
That's WikiTube.

191
00:09:16,330 --> 00:09:18,187
Whatever it is, here's how.
